# Potts, letter Wa - Wh

Wafer.; Laganum.

@AC 9994. "Wafers of what is unleavened anointed with oil" (Exodus 29:2) = what is celestial in the external man; for "wafers" = (this). Explained.

@10079. "And one wafer" (verse 23) = ultimate celestial good; for "a wafer" = celestial good in the external man. Explained.

Wages. See <Stipend>, and <Weigh-Appendere>.

Wail.; Plangere.
Wailing.; Planctus.
See <Howl>, and <Mourn>.

@AC 4060[6]. "Then shall all the tribes of the earth wail" (Matthew 24:30) = that all who are in the good of love and truth of faith will be in grief. ( = a lack of all truth of faith and good of love. @DSS 14[2].) @BE 73.

@4293[3]. (The Israelites) could wail for days.

@4424[3]. "There shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth" (Matthew 25:30) = their state in the other life; "wailing" = their state as to evils.

@4786. Wailing and weeping over the dead, in the Ancient Churches, = interior mourning. Illustrated.

@6539. "They wailed there an exceedingly great and grievous wailing" (Genesis 1:10) = grief... here, the grief of initiation... for before the Knowledges of good and truth... can be implanted in good... there is grief. (Explained.)

@AR 27. "All the tribes of the earth shall wail" (Revelation 1:7) = that this will be when there are no longer any goods and truths in the Church. ( = that the falsities of the Church will oppose. Explained. @AE 39.)

@767[2]. "They shall weep and wail" (Revelation 18:9) = their interior griefs. (To "weep" = mourning because of falsities; and to "wail" = mourning because of evils. Illustrated. @AE 1129[2].)

@AE 617[26]. Lamentation over the destruction of good, is signified by "wailing" (Isaiah 22:12).

@637[8]. Mourning on this account (is signified by) "wail and howl" (Jeremiah 4:8).

@659[4]. "Wail over the multitude of Egypt" (Ezekiel 32:18) = grief on account of their damnation.

@--[22]. "They shall not be bewailed..." (Jeremiah 25:33) = no restoration... "Bewailing" = grief on account of such a state of man; and "no bewailing" = no grief because the man is such that there can be no restoration.

@695[24]. "Over this I will wail and howl" (Micah 1:8) = the grief of the Angels... and of the men of the Church... with whom the Lord is. ( = lamentation over this Church; lamentation over devastated good is signified by "I will make a wailing like dragons" (Micah 1:8)... @AE 714[20].)

Wait. See <Expect>.

Wake. Wakefulness. See <Awake>.

Walk.; Ambulare.
Walking, A.; Ambulatio.
Walk, A.; Ambulacrum.
Promenade, A.; Ambulatorium.
See <Step>, <Wander>, and <Way>.

@AC 247. To "walk on the belly" (Genesis 3:14) = not to be able to look upwards to heavenly things.

@518. To "walk with God" (Genesis 5:22) = the doctrine of faith. ( = to teach and live according to the doctrine of faith; but to "walk with Jehovah" = to live a life of love. @519.) @614.

@519. To "walk" is an accustomed formula which = to live; as to "walk in the law," "in the statutes," "in the Truth." To "walk" properly regards the "way," which is of Truth, consequently which is of faith, that is, the doctrine of faith. Illustrated.

@1379. The walkings... of Spirits... are nothing but changes of state. Explained. @9927[2]. @SE 5646, General article. @LJPost 197, Example(s).

@1612. "Arise, walk through the land" (Genesis 13:17) = that He should thoroughly view the Heavenly Kingdom.

@1629. (The walks -ambulacra- of good and angelic Spirits. Described.) @HH 176. @489[4]. @CL 326. @TCR 280.

@1794. "I am walking childless" (Genesis 15:2) = that there is no internal Church. To "walk" = to live.

@1884. When walking through the streets and fields, and at the same time in speech with Spirits, I knew no otherwise than that I was as awake as at other times, for I walked without a mistake, and was at the same time in vision... But after I had so walked for hours, suddenly I was in the bodily sight, and found myself in a different place, which amazed me. Explained. @HH 441.

@1993. "Walk before Me" (Genesis 17:1) = the truth of faith; for to "walk" = to live according to the truth of faith. (Moreover) "a way," of which "walking" is predicated, = truth.

@2009[5]. To "walk in the name of its god" (Micah 4:5) = profane worship; and to "walk in the name of Jehovah" (Micah 4:5) = true worship.

@3205. "What man is this that walketh in the field to meet us?" (Genesis 24:65) = exploration concerning the Rational, which was in good alone... Its being in good is signified by "walking," that is, meditating, in the field.

@5605[2]. For I have walked in the spirit with and among (Spirits), through many of their abodes, although as to the body I remained in the same place.

@6000[2]. "If any man walk in the day, he stumbleth not; but if any man walk in the night, he stumbleth..." (John 11:9, 10)... To "walk in the day" = to live in truth; and to "walk in the night" = to live in falsity.

@6276. "God, before whom my fathers did walk" (Genesis 48:15) = the Divine from whom internal good and internal truth had life... To "walk" = to live, or to have life.

@7252. (Our Lord seen walking among the inhabitants of Venus.)

@7575. "The fire walked on the earth" (Exodus 9:23) = ... the natural mind possessed (by cupidities) down to its lowest parts. @7577.

@8371. (How the inhabitants of Jupiter walk.) Described. @8372. @8374. @SE 520. @559. @567. @582. @586.

@8420. "Whether they walk in My law..." (Exodus 16:4) = whether they can live the life of truth and good. To "walk" = to live... In the very word to "walk" there is the signification of the spiritual sense, as in very many other words. Explained.

@9028. "If he arise and walk abroad upon his crutch" (Exodus 21:19) = the forces of life in him... To "walk" = to live.

@9212[8]. To "walk" = to live.

@9790. The grandiose style of walking in the First Earth. Described.

@10087[3]. To "walk" = to live according to truths.

@10360[8]. To "walk" = life.

@HH 288[2]. Innocence and peace walk with equal step.

@534[3]. In the other life... everyone walks according to his thoughts which proceed from intention... Illustrated.

@590[end]. Hence it is that... to "walk," etc. in the Word, = progressions of life.

@--. [Swedenborg footnote 1.]. That to "go," and to "walk, with the Lord" = to receive spiritual life, and to live with Him. References.

@DP 60. In the Angelic there is a Knowledge of the way from a walking in it, and a walking in the way through the Knowledge of it.

@AR 75. "Walking in the midst of the seven golden candlesticks" (Revelation 2:1) = from whom is all enlightenment... It is said "walking," because to "walk" = to live. @AE 97.

@137[2]. To "carry the bed, and walk" (Mark 2:9) = to meditate on doctrine.

@153[9]. They love only to walk, sleep, etc.

@167. "They shall walk with Me in white" (Revelation 3:4) = that they will live with the Lord in His Spiritual Kingdom, because they are in truths from Him. To "walk," in the Word, = to live; and to "walk with God" = to live from Him. @--[2]. Illustrated. ( = their spiritual life which they have through the Knowledges of truth and good from the Word. @AE 196.) ( = to follow the Lord, and to live according to the truths of His Word. @TCR 682[2].)

@460. "Which can neither see, hear, nor walk" (Revelation 9:20) = in which there is nothing of spiritual and truly rational life... To "walk" = to live. ( = in which and from which there is nothing of understanding of truth nor perception of good, and thus nothing of spiritual life. @AE 588.)

@706. To "walk naked" (Revelation 16:15) = to live without truths. @AE 1008.

@920. "The nations which are saved shall walk in the light of it" (Revelation 21:19) = that all who are in the good of life, and believe in the Lord, will live therein according to Divine truths, and will see these things within themselves.

@CL 14. The promenade of the palace.

@134[4]. Like sleep-walkers -noctambulones-. Compare @SE 5968.

@267[3]. Such persons... walk as if oppressed with heaviness, with the head hanging down...

@TCR 797[6]. When Melancthon walks, his steps make a knocking sound. Described. Compare @SE 6040.

@SE 1681[2]. The magnificent walks in one of the Earths. Described.

@3116. Some appeared to be standing in their place who told me that they were walking.

@3991. The reflections which cause man... to take care of himself when walking. (Example under reflect.) See also @4221. @4226.

@5583. When the Angels see any Spirit walking below them, they at once perceive from the way in which he walks-via ambulationis, and its windings... what his quality is, and of what he is thinking... No one can learn by heart how to walk according to the heavenly form. Explained.

@5646. When men walk, it is indeed with the body, but it is actually from the will; and the man's walking is in proportion to the amount of will there is present...

@5647. The walkings there are either total or partial changes. Explained.

@5863. From the walkings and the ways -viis- of Rosenstolpe, (his real character) did not appear...

@AE 9[4]. To "walk" = to act and to live.

@97. That to "walk" = to live; and, when predicated of the Lord, life itself, is from the appearances in the Spiritual World; for there all walk according to their life, the evil in those ways only which lead to Hell, and the good in those ways only which lead to Heaven; and therefore all Spirits are Known from the ways in which they walk. Explained.

@--. That to "walk" = to live. Illustrated. @239[20]. @283[8]. @422[13]. @430[16]. @453[11]. @526[11]. @594[10]. @750[23].

@163[7]. "Take up thy bed and walk" (John 5:8) = doctrine, and a life according to it.

@340[13]. To "walk in His ways" (Psalms 128:1) = to do the commandments. ( = to live according to Divine truths. @AE 696[13].)

@514[21]. The Lord's walking upon the sea (Matthew 14; John 6) = the presence and influx of the Lord into these ultimates, and thus life from the Divine in those who are in the ultimates of Heaven; their life from the Divine was represented by the walking of the Lord upon the sea; and their obscure and wavering faith was represented by the fact that Peter, walking upon the sea, began to sink... for to "walk," in the Word, = to live.

@632[11]. To walk on these places (there), is dangerous for those who are merely natural. Explained.

@639[2]. To "walk before God" = to live according to the _esse_ from Him. @687[5].

@687[5]. Walkings and journeyings are movements of man, and therefore = the progression of life, that is, the progression of the thought from the intention of the will.

@717[9]. "Thou hast walked in the midst of the stones of fire" (Ezekiel 28:14) = the truths from the good of love according to which is the life.

@787[2]. In the Word it is said... to "go," and to "walk, after God," "after other gods," "after a leader," and "after many," and by this is signified to follow and acknowledge at heart, and also to be and to live with them, and to be consociated. Illustrated.

@820[7]. To "gird," and to "walk" (John 21:18) = to learn truths, and to live according to them...

@864. To "go," and to "walk, after the Lord" = to acknowledge, obey, do, and live from Him and with Him.

@Char 189. Taking walks as a diversion of charity. Explained.

Wall.; Maceria.

@AR 208. That all things they know and think... are walls of loose stones. Signified, Explained.

@484[7]. A house full of holes and surrounded by a rough wall, seen.

@AE 237[4]. "Wander among the walls" (Jeremiah 49:3) = among truths destroyed through falsities. ( = thought and life from falsities. @435[7].) @637[10].

@--[5]. "The slight wall which they daub with what is untempered" (Ezekiel 13:10) = falsity adopted as a principle, and made to appear as truth...

@--[6]. "I will encompass wall with wall" (Hosea 2:6) = to heap falsities upon falsities.

@543[10]. "Which sit in the walls in the day of cold" (Nahum 3:17) = in truths of the Word which do not appear as truths because they are falsified, and because they are from evil; "walls" = truths which do not appear because they are falsified.

@632[7]. To "take away the hedge, and break down the wall" (Isaiah 5:5) = to falsify, and thus destroy, the truths which defend the Church. Explained.

Wall.; Munis.

@AC 699. This was the "brazen wall." Described. @SE 228.

@6419. "She marcheth upon the wall" (Genesis 49:22) = to fight against falsity. Explained.

@--. "A wall" = the truths of faith, which defend; and, in the opposite sense, the falsities which are destroyed. Illustrated.

@--. "The wall" (of the holy Jerusalem) = the Divine truth which proceeds from the Lord, and derivatively, the truth of faith from the good of charity. Explained.

@7973[4]. ( = the truths of faith which defend the new Church. @8988[4].) 9603[2]. @9643[4]. @9863[2]. @NJHD 1[2]. ( = the truth which protects from the assault of falsities and evils. @HH 73[2]. @307[2].)

@8206. "The waters were a wall to them on their right hand and on their left" (Exodus 14:22) = that they were withheld on all sides from falsities. Explained. @8235.

@8815[end]. "The walls of Jericho" (Joshua 6) = the falsities which defended evils.

@8906[3]. "They run on the wall" (Joel 2:9) = (on) essential falsity.

@DSS 10[end]. "The wall and its foundations" (Revelation 21) = doctrine from the literal sense of the Word.

@36. The Word in the ultimate or natural sense, which is the sense of its letter, is signified by "the wall" of the Holy Jerusalem, the building of which was of jasper... @43.

@AR 655[4]. A city seen there with a wall round it.

@898. "Had a wall great and high" (Revelation 21:12) = the Word in the sense of the letter from which is the doctrine of the New Church. As "the holy city Jerusalem" = the Lord's New Church as to doctrine, its "wall" = the Word in the sense of the letter from which is the doctrine; for this sense protects the spiritual sense... as a wall protects a city and its inhabitants. @TCR 217.

@--. "A wall" = that which protects, and, where the Church is treated of, the Word in the sense of the letter. Illustrated. @904. @909. @911.

@902. "The wall of the city had twelve foundations" (verse 13) = that the Word in the sense of the letter contains all things of the doctrine of the New Church.

@SE 4651. If anyone strikes his hand against a wall... is it the wall that occasions the hurt...

@AE 193[7]. "City," and "wall" = the things of doctrine.

@208[9]. "Against all the walls round about" (Jeremiah 1:15) = to destroy all the protecting truths.

@219[2]. "Walls of brass" (verse 18) = good protecting.

@223[3]. "Walls and bulwarks" (Isaiah 26:1) = truths which protect.

@268[2]. "The wall" of the holy Jerusalem is said to be "of jasper," because "a wall" = Divine truth protecting. @AE 629[7].

@355[16]. "The walls that shall be shaken..." (Ezekiel 26:10) = protecting truths, which are, in general, that there is a God, that the Word is Divine, and that there is an eternal life.

@391[15]. "The walls of her palaces" (Lamentations 2:7) = all protecting truths. "Palaces" = the things of doctrine.

@400[9]. "Wall" = defence.

@410[3]. "Tower," and "wall" (Isaiah 2:15) = falsities of doctrine confirmed.

@430[4]. A "wall" = truths defending against falsities and evils.

@453[12]. "The wall" (Isaiah 22:10) = the truth of doctrine protecting; here, falsified, because without good.

@504[12]. "A wall of fire" (Zechariah 2:5) = protection by the Divine love; for this the Hells cannot approach.

@514[9]. "Lofty tower," and "fortified wall" (Isaiah 2:15) = confirmed principles of falsity.

@700[15]. "The overthrow of the wall of Jericho" = a laying bare to all evil and falsity.

@1145[3]. "The walls" which they shall "destroy" (Ezekiel 26:12) = doctrinal things.

Wall.; Paries.

@AC 739. "A wall plastered with what is untempered" (Ezekiel 13:14) = what is fictitious appearing as truth.

@4050. There appeared walls, but no roof.

@4156[3]. Like one who in the dark sees spots and streaks on a wall... @6400.

@5379. It appeared as if a wall were placed in the way; and when they attempted to overturn the wall, there rose up always a new wall. @SE 993.

@5393[2]. They appear... within a kind of wall. @SE 1066.

@--. There appeared to me a plaster-like wall, with sculpturing... (What it represented.)

@5658[3]. When truth is spoken of... the walls of the rooms where they dwell sparkle with gold and silver.

@10184. The correspondence of the walls, etc. of the altar of incense.

@10185. "Its walls" (Exodus 30:3) = the interiors; for "walls," or "sides," = interior things; for when "the roof" = the inmost, the "walls," which are below, = the interior (or mediate) things. Explained.

@HH 489[5]. The walls of their houses are as it were crystalline, thus transparent, and there appear in them as it were flowing forms which are representative of heavenly things, with perpetual variety. Explained.

@AR 132[end]. "A wall" = truth in ultimates.

@CL 56[2]. The building was divided into two by a transparent wall...

@--[5]. The wife appeared through the crystalline wall.

@76[6]. Many designs were on the walls (of the antechamber). Explained.

@--[7]. Such things are represented on these walls when in meditation about conjugial love...

@231[2]. The lights on the plastered walls presented images of birds of night. @380[4].

@AE 277[5]. The "walls" on which the cherubim were carved (1 Kings 6:29) = the ultimates of Heaven and the Church. @458[3].

@650[66]. "The wall round about," upon which they were seen painted (Ezekiel 8:10) = the interiors everywhere in the natural man; for... "the walls" = the interior things (as distinguished from the inmost and the ultimate ones).

@781[16]. "Who... leans with his hand upon the wall, and a serpent bites him" (Amos 5:19) = that when such a one consults the Word in the sense of the letter... he does not see that evils are perverting it.

@811[6]. To "bring out through the wall the vessels of migration, in the dark..." (Ezekiel 12:5, 6) = that all the truths of doctrine from the Word had been cast out... "The wall" = the ultimate which encompasses and protects truths; and the ultimate of doctrine is the sense of the letter... which is called "a wall" because it contains and encloses the spiritual sense.

@827[7]. "Men painted upon the wall" (Ezekiel 23:14) = (doctrinals which outwardly appear to be truths, although inwardly they are profane). "A painted wall" = the appearance of the doctrinal things in externals.

@1145[8]. "The wall out of which the stone crieth" (Habakkuk 2:11) = a man devoid of truths, and who consequently wishes to be instructed, from what is false.

@LJPost 331. The Spirits themselves can be passed into the houses through the walls...

Wallerius.; Wallerius. @SE 4830.

Wallet.; Mantica.

@AC 5497. "It was in the mouth of his wallet" (Genesis 42:27) = that they were... stored up in the threshold of the exterior Natural. @5657.

@5500. "A wallet" = the exterior Natural. @5661. @5733. @5767.

@5656. "When we opened our wallets" (Genesis 43:21) = introspection into the exterior Natural.

@5733. "Fill the wallets of the men with food" (Genesis 44:1) = (influx) into the Natural with the good of truth.

@5735. "And put the silver of each one in the mouth of his wallet" (Genesis 44:1) = over and above with truth anew in the exterior Natural.

@5767. "They took down every man his wallet to the earth" (verse 11) = that they brought the things which were in the Natural down to sensuous things.

Wan. See <Ghastly>.

Wander. See <Error>.

Wander.; Aberrare.

@AE 710[17]. "The wicked go astray (or wander from the way) from the belly" (Psalms 58:3) = that they have receded from truths to falsities.

Wander.; Exspatiari. Spatiari.
Ranging about, A.; Exspatiatio.

@AC 5096[end]. In thought they can... range at large through the whole Heaven.

@HH 270[4]. (Such) can walk about in the paradises...

@DP 289. To which their thoughts were wont to range.

@SE 2318. When I suffered my ideas to range at large...

@2361[2]. In order that those in the Society may be restrained from wandering about any further.

@2367[6]. Although thought from the spirit ranges about outside of him...

@3416[2]. He ranged about in the net... Concerning (this) ranging about -exspatiatione-...

@3497. They acted as if they were ranging about in an open field (of thought).

@4139. a. So with the thought, which can range into the universe...

@5312. They are tortured because they cannot wander forth from the body by the thoughts.

@5902. There is given to every Spirit the opportunity to go out of his own Society, and wander around; but they who love uses for the sake of uses never want to do it...

@AE 8[2]. We may not as yet expatiate upon this subject.

@775[3]. The mind (then) has an extension into everything of the whole body, and ranges there through its forms, as the thoughts and affections of the Angels do into the Societies of the universal Heaven. @837[2], Explained. @DLove 13[4].

@783[2]. If there were room to expatiate so far...

@786[12]. For spiritual thought can range into innumerable things into which natural thought cannot.

@DLove 15[2]. Works keep the lower mind as in... bonds, and prevent it from wandering into the ravings of these cupidities.

Wander.; Vagari. Divagari. Extravagari. Pervagari.
Wandering, A.; Vagatio.
Wandering.; Vagabundus. Vagus.
Wanderer.; Vagus.

@AC 330. The derivative falsity and evil is "a wanderer -vagum- and fugitive in the earth" (Genesis 4:12).

@382. To be "a wanderer and fugitive in the earth" = not to know what is true and good.

@--. To "wander blind in the streets" (Lamentations 4:14) = not to know what is good and true.

@--[2]. To "wander to drink waters" (Amos 4:8) = to seek what is true. @AE 532[8].

@391. Those who have divested themselves of all charity, wander and flee (homeless).

@398. "Nod" is a word which means to be a wanderer and a fugitive.

@957. Those who have contracted a nature of speaking one thing and thinking another... wander around...

@3240[4]. Desolation is described by to "wander before swords..." (Isaiah 21:15).

@--. Celestial things... are signified by... to "meet the wanderer -vagabundum- with bread" (verse 14).

@3708[7]. To "wander from sea to sea" (Amos 8:12) = to seek where there are Knowledges.

@4051[end]. (The Spirits of the isthmus of the brain) are of the wandering Societies. @5189. @SE 3822.

@4453. "Wander through -pervagamini- the land, trading" (Genesis 34:10) = to enter into the Knowledges of good and truth.

@4793. Wandering Spirits of the infernal crew who... strive to enter into man's taste. Described.

@5180[end]. They do not allow another to wander -divagari- from his own idea...

@--. These Spirits (of the province of the chyle) are among the wandering Spirits. @SE 1136.

@6697[end]. These satellites range round their respective globes...

@6925. The Spirits of Mercury... wander through the universe. Explained.

@SE 2820. This is why such wander hither and thither in the World of Spirits.

@3093. There are bonds to keep them from roaming extravagentur (into new evil).

@3149. An indescribable fear withheld him from going beyond limits -extravagaretur-.

@3835[end]. A Society of these evil Spirits was represented by...

@4190. Beyond the sphere (of these particulars) the thoughts and speech cannot go -extravagari-.

@AE 654[55]. "Woe unto them, for they have wandered from Me" (Hosea 7:13) = a turning away from the truths which are from the Word.

@730[31]. These things were represented by the wandering... of the sons of Israel in the wilderness.

@817[3]. In consequence of the death of charity the Church perishes, which is signified by... "becoming a wanderer and a fugitive;" for when faith is separated from charity, truth is successively turned into falsity...

@1089[2]. Whereby his mind becomes wandering -vaga- and unsettled.

Wander about.; Circumvagari.
Wanderer about, A.; Circumvagator.

@AC 958. Troops of Spirits who wander about, and who are dreaded. @5389.

@6696. Spirits of Mercury who are allowed to wander about... @6925, Explained.

@7997[2]. When these (Spirits) are allowed to wander about, which happens at their first arrival in the other life...

@10785[2]. From our Earth there are some who wander about there...

@SE 4321. Paul is among such troops as wander about.

@DLove 12. Not a lazy wanderer about.

Want. See <Fail-Deficere>, and <Need-Egestas>.

Want.; Avere.

@HH 399[end]. He wants or covets the goods of another.

@450. He wants to depart from the celestial Angels.

@CL 208[5]. A sign that we want to divulge things still more secret.

@SE 4253. Spirits... desire and want this thing or that according to their nature and state.

Want.; Carere.

@AC 9323[2]. To "want bread and water" (Ezekiel 4:17) = to be deprived of the good of love and truth of faith. ( = to be vastated as to the good of love and as to the truth of doctrine. @AE 633[3].)

Wanting, To be.; Deesse.

@AC 5851[end]. It is never wanting that... @DP 294[6].

@8474. "There was not wanting to the few" (Exodus 16:18) = a just ratio.

@DLW 389. If any part were wanting in man... there would be wanting something of determination...

@DP 329[3]. To no man is there wanting a Knowledge of the means...

@AE 893[4]. "One thing thou lackest" (Mark 10:21). Explained.

Wantonness.; Petulantia.
Wanton.; Petulans.
Wantonly.; Petulanter.

@AC 1113. He chastises the girls whenever in thought they break out into such wantonnesses.

@5180[2]. Some of them are modest, others are impudent. Explained.

@TCR 74[2]. How impudent this is!

@SE 4681. Some are wantonly evil.

@--[2]. They reject those who are wanton.

Wapping.; Wapping. @LJPost 292.

War.; Bellum.
See <Army>, <Battle>, <Victory>, and <Weapons>.

@AC 1651. The wars described in Genesis 14. = the Lord's combats of temptations. @1659[2]. @1663. @1664.

@1659[2]. In the Most Ancient times, many things were represented by wars, which were called "the wars of Jehovah," which = the combats of the Church, and of those who belonged to the Church, that is, their temptations, which are nothing but combats and wars with the evils in one's self, and consequently with the diabolical crew which excites the evils, and endeavours to destroy the Church and the man of the Church. By "the wars," in the Word, nothing else is signified... @1664. Fully illustrated.

@1664[6]. That it is the Lord alone who sustains all the combat, and who overcomes... is everywhere represented by the wars which the sons of Israel waged against the nations. Illustrated... For the wars there... all represented the Lord's combats with Hell; and consequently those of His Church, and of the men of the Church. Further Illustrated.

@--[11]. For the same reason the descendants of Jacob called their wars the wars of Jehovah. And the same was the case in the Ancient Churches, among whom were books called "The wars of Jehovah" (Numbers 21:14, 15); which were written in a manner not unlike that in which the wars are treated of in this chapter; but the wars of the Church were signified. @2686. @2897. @3268[7].

@1788. As "war" = temptations, so all the weapons of war = some specific thing of temptation, and of defence against evils and falsities. Example(s). @2686[2]. @2799[5]. @3448.

@3353[2]. "Wars and rumours of wars" (Matthew 24:6) = debates and disputes about truths, which are "wars" in the spiritual sense.

@4599[5]. To "make war" (Luke 14:31) = to fight from truths; for temptations are treated of.

@6656. "Wars" (Exodus 1:10) = combats concerning truths and falsities, or spiritual combats. @7351[2].

@8054[3]. This is meant by, "There was war in Heaven..." @8295[2].

@8096. To "repent when they see war" (Exodus 13:17) = to decline from truth in consequence of assaults. Explained.

@8117[end]. When I wanted to say that in this Earth there are wars, etc. (the Spirits of Jupiter) turned away...

@8273. "Jehovah is a man of war" (Exodus 15:3) = that the Lord will protect against all the evils and falsities which are from the Hells... for the Lord alone fights for man... The Lord is called "a man of war" chiefly from the fact that when He was in the world. He, alone, that is, from Himself, fought against the Hells... and since then (from the fact) that having thus conquered the Hells, and been made justice. He from His Divine power protects men, and this continually, especially in the combats of temptations. Illustrated.

@--[4]. When "war" is mentioned in the Word, there is meant spiritual war, which is against falsities and evils, or, what is the same, against the devil, that is, the Hells.

@--. Of the wars, or combats, of the Lord against the Hells, it treats in both the historical and prophetical things of the Word; and in like manner of the wars and combats of the Lord for man. With the Ancients... "The Book of the Wars of Jehovah" (treated of) the Lord's combats and victories over the Hells when He was in the world; and also of His subsequent perpetual combats and victories in favour of man, His Church, and Kingdom. Explained. @9942[5]. @AR 11.

@8295[2]. On wars in the other life. See <Combat>.

@8313[3]. "Prepared as a man for war" (Jeremiah 6:23) = the cupidity of assaulting truth.

@8624. "Jehovah Nissi" = the Lord's continual war and protection against those who are in the falsity of interior evil. Explained. @8626, Explained.

@9182[6]. "War" = spiritual combat. References.

@9391[16]. "He hath scattered the peoples that long for wars" (Psalms 68:30)... The desire to attack and destroy the Church with its truths is meant by to "long for wars." ( = reasonings against truths. @AE 627[13].)

@9393[3]. "Man of war" (Ezekiel 39:20) = truth fighting against falsity.

@9396[11]. "Wars" = combats concerning truths. References.

@9642[7]. The alternations which the Church would undergo until it would perish, are described by the various successes of the "war" (in Daniel 11).

@10455. "There is a voice of war in the camp" (Exodus 32:17) = an attack on the truth and good which are of the Church by the falsities and evils which are from Hell.

@--. For "war" = the combat of truth from good with falsity from evil; and, in the opposite sense, the combat of falsity from evil against truth from good. (For "war," in the spiritual sense, is nothing else; and such combats are signified by "the wars" in the historicals of the Word, and also by "the wars" in the propheticals. Illustrated. @--[3].)

@10540[6]. "No strength in war" (Isaiah 3:25) = not any resistance against evil and falsity.

@DLord 5. "The day of war," etc. = the advent of the Lord to Judgment. Illustrated.

@14[9]. As the Lord alone conquered the Hells, with no aid from any Angel, He is called "a Hero," and "a Man of wars" (Isaiah 42:15)... "a Hero of war" etc. (Psalms 24:8).

@--[11]. In the historicals of the Word, like things are represented by the wars of the sons of Israel with various nations; for... everything written there is written about the Lord.

@DSS 103. "The Wars of Jehovah," in the Ancient Word, as in ours, are meant and described in reference to the Lord's combats with Hell, and His victory over it, when He should come into the world; and the same combats are meant and described in many places of the historicals of our Word, as in the wars of Joshua with the nations of the land of Canaan, and in the wars of the judges and kings of Israel. @TCR 265. @279.

@DFaith 50. For all the wars described in the Word, involve and signify, in the spiritual sense, spiritual wars.

@DP 251. That the worshipper of self and nature confirms himself against the Divine Providence when he thinks that wars are permitted... General article.

@--. It is not of the Divine Providence that wars take place, because they are united with homicide, depredation, violence, cruelty, and other enormous evils which are diametrically contrary to Christian charity; but still they cannot but be permitted, because, since the time of the Most Ancients... the life's love of men has become of such a nature that it wants to exercise dominion over others, and at last over all; it also wants to possess the wealth of the world, and at last all of it. These two loves cannot be kept in bonds, for it is according to the Divine Providence that everyone be allowed to act from freedom according to reason; and without permissions man cannot be led by the Lord from evil... for unless evils were permitted to break forth, man would not see them... and therefore could not be led to resist them. Hence it is that evils cannot be prevented by any Providence; for they would remain shut in, and... would spread and consume all that is vital in man... It is for this reason that there are lesser and greater wars; lesser, between the possessors of farms or estates and their neighbours, and greater between monarchs of kingdoms and their neighbours. Whether a war be lesser or greater makes no difference, except that a lesser one is kept within limits by the laws of the nation, and a greater one by the laws of nations; both the lesser one and the greater one want to transgress, but the lesser one cannot, and the greater one can, but still not beyond what is possible.

@--. That the greater wars... are not prevented by the Lord, at the beginning, or in the course of them, but only at the end, when the power of the one or the other party has been so weakened that it is in danger of destruction, there are many reasons for, which are stored up in the treasury of the Divine wisdom. Some of these have been revealed to me, among which is this: that all wars... are representative of states of the Church in Heaven, and are correspondences. Such were all the wars described in the Word, and such also are all wars at this day... When the Sons of Israel, who represented the Church, fell away from the precepts and statutes into the evils represented by these nations (enumerated.) ... they were punished by the nation (which represented the particular evil into which they had fallen). Example(s).

@--[4]. Like things are represented by wars at this day, wherever they are; for all things which take place in the natural world correspond to spiritual things in the Spiritual World; and all spiritual things concern the Church... There are kingdoms in Christendom, which answer to (the several nations with which the Israelites carried on wars). But the quality of the Church on earth, and what the evils are into which it falls, and on account of which it is punished by means of wars, cannot be at all seen in the natural world... but it is seen in the Spiritual World, where... all are conjoined according to their various states. The conflicts of these in the Spiritual World correspond to the wars [which take place]...

@--[5]. That the wars which take place in the world are ruled by the Divine Providence... is acknowledged by a spiritual man, but not by a natural man...

@--[6]. The Divine Providence which is called Fortune is in the smallest particulars of even trivial things... and most certainly in the affairs of war. Moreover, successes and affairs in war which are happily carried out, are called... the Fortune of war; and this is the Divine Providence, acting especially in the plans and meditations of the general...

@252[2]. The evil (also) perform uses... and with more ardour than the good, especially in wars, because an evil man is more crafty... and, from the love of glory, is in the delight of killing and plundering... his enemies; (whereas) a good man is prudent and zealous only to defend, and rarely... to invade. Further explained.

@AR 52. "Wars," in the Word, = spiritual wars, which are those of truth against falsity, and of falsity against truth; and therefore by the weapons of war are signified such things as are used to fight with in these wars. Example(s).

@431. "Like horses prepared for war" (Revelation 9:7) = that because they can reason they appeared to themselves as fighting from the understanding of truth... "War" = spiritual war, which is waged by means of reasonings and argumentations. @AE 552.

@437. To "run to war" (Revelation 9:7) = the ardour of fighting (in spiritual combat). @AE 558.

@500. "The beast... shall make war with them" (Revelation 11:7) = that (these) will set themselves in opposition to and assault the two essentials of the New Church. ( = an assault from infernal love. @AE 650.)

@--[5]. That "wars," in the Word, = spiritual wars, which are assaults on truth, and are waged by means of reasonings from falsities. Illustrated.

@548. "There was war in Heaven..." (Revelation 12:7) = the falsities of the former Church fighting against the truths of the New Church. Explained. ( = a combat of falsity against truth, and of truth against falsity. Explained. @AE 734.)

@--. "War" = spiritual war, which is that of falsity against truth, and of truth against falsity.

@586. "It was granted to him to make war with the saints" (Revelation 13:7) = that they assaulted the Divine truths of the Word. "War" = spiritual war, which is that of falsity against truth, and of truth against falsity; hence to "make war" = to assault, ( = a combat with those who are in truths from good. @AE 802.) @AR 704.

@833. "The beast and the kings of the earth gathered together to make war with Him that sat on the horse..." (Revelation 19:19) = that all (such) will attack the Lord's Divine truths...

@858. "Gog and Magog, to gather them together to war" (Revelation 20:8) = those in merely external worship... excited against those who have worshipped the Lord.

@TCR 407[2]. Wars which have as an end the protection of our country and Church, are not contrary to charity; the end from which [they are waged] declares whether there is charity [in them] or not.

@SE 2576. What is meant by their "learning wars;" [in other words] why the faithful have to undergo persecutions and temptations. Explained.

@4346[2]. So in war, the end is victory, and thus the common good... there is no mercy towards those who fall, because there is mercy in the end of [saving] many.

@4426. In the other life, there are... other wars, namely, against evils and the infernals.

@4884. (Charles XII) declared war against the Lord.

@AE 131. "Wars," in the Word, = spiritual wars, which are those of truths against falsities, and of falsities against truths. @283[15]. @734[2], Illustrated.

@315[6]. "Their young men smitten with the sword in war" (Jeremiah 18:21) = truths destroyed by the assaults of falsity.

@355[2]. "Ye shall be satiated... with every man of war" (Ezekiel 39:20) = with the truth from good which destroys falsity. @617[25]. @650[48].

@--[28]. "As a horse of glory in war" (Zechariah 10:3) = the understanding of Divine truth fighting against evils and falsities, which it will destroy.

@357[4]. "God teacheth my hands war" (Psalms 18:34). By "war," here, is signified war in a spiritual sense, which is war against evils and falsities. This is the war that God teaches.

@--[8]. "The grievousness of war" (Isaiah 21:15) = an assault.

@--[28]. "Jehovah maketh wars to cease even to the extremity of the earth" (Psalms 46:9) = [that He will cause to cease] all combat and all dissension from the primes to the ultimates of the truth of the Church... "Wars" = spiritual combats, which, here, are those of falsity against the truth and the good of the Church.

@--[30]. "I will break the bow, and the sword, and war, from the earth" (Hosea 2:18) = that because of conjunction with the Lord there shall exist no combat of falsity against truth... "War" = combat.

@386[16]. "The hands of the sword in war" (Job 5:20) = temptation as to the understanding of truth; "war" = temptation, or combat against falsities. @388[18].

@395[10]. "Men returning from war" (Micah 2:8) = those who have shaken off falsities; "war" = the combat of truth against falsity. ( = those who have been in temptations, and have fought against falsities. @555[8].)

@403[12]. "Nation shall not lift up sword against nation, neither shall they learn war any more" (Micah 4:3) = that in the (Celestial) Kingdom there shall be no disputation about truths... For such have truths inscribed on their hearts, and therefore do not dispute about them.

@433[33]. To "take away the strong man and the man of war" (Isaiah 3:2) = to take away all resistance against evils and falsities. @727[12], Explained.

@538[10]. "The men of war" (Ezekiel 27:27) = those who defend.

@573[12]. The collision and combat at the end of the Church are described by (the "war" between the kings in Dan. 11).

@652[8]. "Men of war" = truths fighting against falsities; and that there will be no defence of truth against falsities, is signified by, "All the men of war shall be cutoff" (Jeremiah 49:26; 50:30).

@654[65]. "Where we shall see no war" (Jeremiah 42:14) = that there will then be no infestation by falsities and evils, and no temptations; "war" = infestation and combat by falsities and evils.

@684[39]. "Even unto the end of the war desolations are determined" (Daniel 9:26) = even until there is no combat between truth and falsity... "War" = combat between truth and falsity; and "desolation," the last state of the Church, when there is no longer any truth, but mere falsity.

@768. "He went away to make war with the remnant of her seed" (Revelation 12:17) = thence from a life of evil an ardent endeavour to assault the truths of doctrine of the New Church. ( = to attack and assault by means of reasonings from falsities. @AR 565.)

@817[6]. All the wars which the sons of Israel waged with the Philistines represented the combats of the spiritual man with the natural man, and thus the combats of truth conjoined with good with truth separated from good, which in itself is falsity.

@Char 164. On charity in a Commander-in-chief... He does not love war, but peace; even in war he continually loves peace. He does not go to war except for the protection of his country... but when the war has commenced, he is the aggressor, when aggression is defence.

