Wares. See <Merchandise>.

Warfare.; Militia.
See <Soldier>.

@AC 1664[7]. As the priests represented the Lord, who alone fights for man, their office is called "warfare." Illustrated in @5335[2].

@2276[4]. Under <Thirty>, see this reference.

@3448. Hence by "warfare," and "war," are signified the things of spiritual warfare and war. Illustrated.

@7236. After they have exercised spiritual warfare. Treated of.

@10225[10]. To "go forth for warfare" (Numbers 26:2) = to go forth into combats against the evils and falsities which are from Hell.

@AR 500[6]. Therefore the ministry of the Levites was called "warfare." Illustrated.

@SE 1397. Those in warfare who love nothing but slaughter and spoils...

@AE 734[14]. That "war" = spiritual war, which is against infernal things, is evident from the fact that the offices and ministries of the Levites about the Tent are called "warfare." Illustrated, Explained.

@--. Thus the priesthood is warfare, but warfare against falsities and evils.

@1115[3]. "Her warfare is fulfilled" (Isaiah 40:2) = combat against evils.

Warmth.; Incalescentia.
Warm, To grow.; Incalescere.

@AC 2146. "As the day grew warm" (Genesis 18:1) = from love. Explained.

@--. All affection is signified by "warmth," even in common discourse.

@3527[3]. To "grow warm" (Isaiah 57:5) is predicated of evil.

@4019. "The flocks grew warm at the rods" (Genesis 30:39) = the effect from His Own power; for to "grow warm" = the effect of the affection.

@4029. To "grow warm" = the ardour and effect of affection; (and therefore it = ) the things which are spontaneous. Explained. @4031.

@4030. "That it might grow warm" (verse 41) = that they might be conjoined. @4082.

@4581[7]. To "grow warm with gods" (Isaiah 57:5) = with concupiscences of what is false. ( = the ardour of worship. @10137[7].)

@6832[3]. Under <Heat>, see this reference.

@7356[2]. To "grow warm," etc. = cupidities.

@8487. "The sun grew warm, and it melted" (Exodus 16:21) = that (the good of truth) vanishes according to the degree of increasing concupiscence. Explained.

@9278[4]. When in externals, man... grows warm from the world, and grows cold to Heaven.

@HH 134[end]. That love is heat from a spiritual origin, is evident from man's warmth according to love; for man is kindled and grows warm according to the quantity and quality of it... @567. @DLW 95. @379[2]. @CL 380[12].

@DLW 112. As to the interiors of their minds, men grow warm from that Sun.

@148. Hence it is said... that they grow warm with God.

@CL 225[end]. When the man grows warm -calescit-.

@270[end]. That it may grow warm -calescat- from an illicit fire.

@AE 411[26]. To "inflame one's self with gods under every green tree" (Isaiah 57:5) = to worship God from every falsity that occurs; to "inflame one's self with gods" = ardent worship.

@601[11]. The ardour of those who unite in doing this, is signified by, "when they are heated I will set their feasts" (Jeremiah 51:39).

Warn.; Admonere.
Warning, A.; Admonitio.

@AC 6737. A warning from the Divine. Signified.

@7220. A warning to those who infest. Signified. @7228. @7237. @7243.

@7273. "I will multiply My signs and My prodigies" = warnings of every kind. Explained. @7795, Explained.

@7295[2]. This prodigy = the first warning to those who infest, that they should desist. Explained.

@7306. That it is the Divine who warns them to desist from infestations. Signified.

@7652. A warning by those who are in fear. Signified and (Explained.)

@8839. A warning still. Signified, Explained. @8840.

@AR 211. A warning that they should procure from the Lord... the good of love. Signified, Explained.

@628. A warning that they should not do evils. Signified, Explained.

@SE 2149. Although such a continual admonition inflows...

