@AC 24. "Let there be an expanse in the midst of the waters, and let it distinguish between the waters and the waters" (Genesis 1:6)... The Knowledges in the internal man are called "the waters above the expanse"; and the scientifics of the external man, "the waters under the expanse." Explained. ( = spiritual things in the Rational and the Natural. @3623[2].) ( = memory truths, and the interior truths of faith. @9340[3].) @9596[end].

@27[end]. These Knowledges (in the external memory) are "the waters gathered together to one place," and "are called seas" (verses 9-10).

@28. "Waters," in the Word, = Knowledges and scientifics. Illustrated.

@57[2]. "The waters going out of the sanctuary" (Ezekiel 47:12) = the life and mercy of the Lord. ( = the truths which confer intelligence. @6502[5].)

@382[2]. To "wander to drink waters" (Amos 4:8) = to seek for what is true.

@623. "They shall drink their waters in desolation" (Ezekiel 12:19) = spiritual things to which they have done violence.

@680[3]. "Water" (John 4) = the spiritual things of faith.

@739. "A flood of waters" (Genesis 7) = the beginning of temptation as to intellectual things... For "waters" = especially the spiritual things of man, or the intellectual things of faith, and also the falsities which are the opposites of them. Illustrated.

@789. That "the waters" (of the Flood) = falsities.

@790. Illustrated. @871. @877.

@790. "Waters," in the Word, in general, = what is spiritual, that is, what is intellectual, rational, and scientific; and therefore also the contrary things...

@794. "The waters were strengthened very exceedingly upon the earth" (verse 19) = that persuasions of what is false thus increased.

@847. "The waters had receded from upon the earth, in going and returning" (Genesis 8:3) = fluctuations between truth and falsity. Explained.

@857. "The waters were going and decreasing" (verse 5) = that falsities began to disappear. @887.

@1678[3]. "Waters," in the internal sense = spiritual things, which are truths.

@2129. I heard a sound as of many waters. Explained. @AR 484[7]. @TCR 390[2].

@2161. "Let a little water be brought" (Genesis 18:4) = ... that the Divine should let itself down nearer to His intellectual things. Explained.

@2240[5]. "They found no waters" (Jeremiah 14:3) = no Knowledges of truth.

@2466[12]. "Waters" = Knowledges. References. @2967[3]. @3419.

@2674. "(Abraham) took bread, and a bottle of water" (Genesis 21:14) = good and truth. Explained.

@2681. "The water was consumed out of the bottle" (verse 15) = the desolation of truth.

@2702[4]. "The afflicted and the needy seek waters, and there are none" (Isaiah 41:17) = the desolation of truth. ( = those who long for the Knowledges of good and truth. @10227[23].)

@--[5]. "Living water" (John 4:10) = truth itself.

@--[9]. "Rivers of living water" (John 7:38), and "living fountains of waters" (Revelation 7:17) = truths which are from the Lord, that is, from His Word.

@--[9]. "Waters," "streams," "lakes," and "springs of waters" (Isaiah 35) = truths which were for refreshment and joy to those in vastation.

@--[12]. That "waters" = truths, spiritual, rational, and scientific. Illustrated.

@--[13]. It is spiritual waters that are meant; that is, the spiritual things which are of truth.

@2703. "(Hagar) filled her bottle with water" (Genesis 21:19) = truths thence.

@2781[4]. "That sow beside all waters" (Isaiah 32:20) = those who suffer themselves to be instructed in spiritual things.

@2928[2]. "Bread," and "water" (Ezekiel 12:19) = charity and faith, or good and truth.

@3058. To "draw waters" = instruction, and also the consequent enlightenment; for "waters" = the truths of faith; and therefore to "draw waters" = to be instructed in the truths of faith, and thus to be enlightened. Illustrated. @3094 .

@--[end]. Moreover, "the drawers of waters," in the Jewish Church, represented those who are continually wanting to know truths merely for the sake of knowing them, and without caring about any use.

@3068. "Water" = truth. @9396[end], References.

@3079[4]. "Water shall flow from his buckets" (Numbers 24:7) = that truths will do so from Knowledges.

@3089. "Let me... sip a little water from thy pitcher" (Genesis 24:17) = an inquiry as to whether anything of truth from this source could be conjoined.

