@8299. "In the vast waters" (Exodus 15:10) = whelmed about by an immense number of falsities.

@8347. "They went three days in the wilderness, and found no waters" (Exodus 15:22) = that truths were lacking, and at last utterly.

@8349. "They could not drink the waters on account of their bitterness" (Exodus 15:23) = that truths appeared undelightful to them, because devoid of the affection of good; for to "drink waters" = to receive truths, and apply them under good. Explained.

@8355. To "cast wood into waters" = to affect truths with good.

@8356. "The waters were made sweet" (Exodus 15:25) = that in this way truths are made delightful.

@8368. "There were twelve springs of waters" (Exodus 15:27) = truths in all abundance.

@8370. "They encamped there beside the waters" (Exodus 15:27) = that after temptation the truths of faith are put in order by means of the good of love. Explained.

